    {
      "id": "claim_0a5cf85e53464f16a101823ae7412789",
      "statement": "`rusty session start` starts the back end unit and then, unless the app unit is already active, refuses while a `rusty` process outside the unit is running (naming its pid), otherwise imports the display variables the user manager lacks and starts the app unit, ending with the status; `stop` stops the app unit alone and says the back end keeps serving; `status` prints both units' state, whether an MCP `initialize` posted to the port is answered 200, and the app's process ids.",
